chat-test` may match zero test files or error on opening a literal path, on a Node version this project claims to support (>=20). The repo already solved this for the analogous TypeScript project: `projects/realtime-agent/src/agent/package.json` uses a dedicated `node scripts/run-agent-tests.mjs` runner instead of a shell glob, precisely to make discovery deterministic. The current approach happened to pass in the implementer's environment but is fragile and inconsistent with that convention.\\n\\n## What must be true to close\\n- Test discovery is deterministic across a clean checkout on the declared minimum Node (>=20) and the default npm shell — e.g. an explicit file list, a small runner script (as in realtime-agent), or `--test` with a non-globstar-dependent pattern.\\n- `make sheaf-chat-test` reliably executes all `tests/*.test.ts` outputs (currently 9 tests) rather than silently running zero.\\nEOF\\n)\\\"\", \"description\": \"Create issue: test glob fragility\"}, \"name\": \"Bash\", \"type\": \"tool_use\"}], \"context_management\": null, \"id\": \"msg_01CGrna8vsAuZGXTyr9WrWaK\", \"model\": \"claude-opus-4-8\", \"role\": \"assistant\", \"stop_details\": null, \"stop_reason\": null, \"stop_sequence\": null, \"type\": \"message\", \"usage\": {\"cache_creation\": {\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\": 1192, \"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\": 0}, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 1192, \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 79003, \"inference_geo\": \"not_available\", \"input_tokens\": 2, \"output_tokens\": 35, \"service_tier\": \"standard\"}}, \"parent_tool_use_id\": null, \"session_id\": \"1b26321b-d55f-4609-88ad-ae089fd1e9f6\", \"type\": \"assistant\", \"uuid\": \"9f94eee0-a35c-4ec5-812a-4c81523a5ed9\"}, \"provider_thread_id\": \"1b26321b-d55f-4609-88ad-ae089fd1e9f6\", \"role\": \"polisher_reviewer\", \"schema_version\": 1, \"sequence\": 2622, \"step\": 14, \"thread\": \"sheaf-chat_main_0000_sheaf_chat_quest_0000_slice_0001_polisher_reviewer\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-08T19:53:23Z